00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.270
JOE: All children reach a range
of developmental milestones

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.800
between birth and adulthood.

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:09.079
Children with autism, however,
may reach some on time, or even

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.820
early, but lose ground later or
not reach some milestones at all.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:17.430
Some may develop skills that are
very advanced, but not the useful

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.849
ones they need in everyday life.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:22.830
BETH: here are, a few developmental
markers that are most likely

00:00:23.009 --> 00:00:26.050
and most obvious when a child
has autism spectrum disorder.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:31.450
Problems such as working simple toys, not
speaking in sentences, not understanding

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.569
simple instructions, not playing as
others and the lack of eye contact.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.190
JOE: The physical changes of
puberty can have an alarming

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.110
